<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 29 January, from 1676 to 1916.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1676 <span class="tih-ago">350 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Feodor III becomes Tsar of Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of Tsar Alexei, his sickly 14-year-old son Feodor succeeded him. In a short reign he abolished the system of ranking nobles by ancestry, paving the way for his half-brother Peter the Great.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1820 <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George III dies at Windsor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Blind and suffering from mental illness, George III died after a reign of almost 60 years, which had seen the loss of America and victory over Napoleon. His son the Prince Regent became George IV.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1845 <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edgar Allan Poe's 'The Raven' is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Poe's poem of a grieving lover and a talking bird appeared in the New York Evening Mirror. It made him famous almost overnight, though it earned him little money.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1886 <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Karl Benz files a patent for his motor car</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benz applied for a German patent on a 'vehicle powered by a gas engine', his three-wheeled Motorwagen. It is generally regarded as the first practical petrol-driven automobile.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1900 <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The American League of baseball is organised</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ban Johnson reorganised a minor league as the American League, with eight teams. It declared itself a major league in 1901 and met the National League in the first World Series in 1903.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1916 <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zeppelin raid kills civilians in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A German airship bombed eastern Paris, killing more than twenty people in the Ménilmontant area. It was the last Zeppelin raid on the city, which strengthened its air defences.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
